# Copy to `.env.local` for development. Never commit a filled-in copy —
# `.gitignore` excludes `.env*`, and `.env.example` is the documented exception.
#
# AUDIT.md N-12.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Site (required in production)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Canonical origin, no trailing slash. While this is unset the site emits
# `noindex` and robots.txt disallows everything, deliberately, so that
# preview deployments cannot be indexed (AUDIT.md Q-06).
#   e.g. https://55candles.example
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Email — Resend (AUDIT.md B-17, B-20)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The provider is Resend, reached over its HTTP API — no SDK. Two variables make
# email work at all; the other two decide where our copies land.
#
# Until BOTH of the first two are set: /api/contact returns 503 and the form tells
# the customer to phone, and a placed order is stored but nobody is emailed (the
# server log says so loudly, and the admin shows a warning). Nothing silently
# pretends to have sent.

# Resend API key, from resend.com → API Keys. Starts `re_`.
EMAIL_PROVIDER_API_KEY=

# The From address. MUST be on a domain verified with Resend (Domains → Add),
# which means adding its DKIM/SPF records to the domain's DNS. A display name is
# allowed and recommended:
#   EMAIL_FROM="55° candles <orders@55candles.com>"
EMAIL_FROM=

# Where contact-form enquiries are delivered. Any mailbox — it does not have to
# be on the verified domain. Several addresses, comma-separated, go in one email
# rather than one each:
#   CONTACT_EMAIL_TO=anna@gmail.com,boris@gmail.com
CONTACT_EMAIL_TO=

# Where new orders are announced, if that differs from the address above. The
# notification carries the items, the phone number and the delivery point, so the
# parcel can be packed without opening the admin. Falls back to CONTACT_EMAIL_TO.
# ORDER_EMAIL_TO=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Admin (AUDIT.md Phase 7)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The order panel lives at /admin, outside the localised site, and is Bulgarian
# only. One shared password, because the shop is one or two people.
#
# While this is unset there is no way in — an unset password is "no admin", never
# "any password works". Use something long; the login form is throttled per IP but
# that is a speed bump, not a defence.
ADMIN_PASSWORD=

# Optional. Signs the admin session cookie. Defaults to ADMIN_PASSWORD, which
# means changing the password logs everyone out — usually what you want. Set this
# separately only if you want sessions to survive a password change.
# ADMIN_SESSION_SECRET=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Invoices (AUDIT.md Phase 6)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# WHO DRAWS UP THE ФАКТУРА, by name. Required for the admin's "Издай фактура"
# button; nothing else in the shop reads it.
#
# A primary accounting document carries the name of the natural person who made
# it (ЗСч), and `company.manager` in `src/lib/company.ts` is deliberately null
# because the owner does not publish their name on the open web. An invoice is not
# the open web — it goes to one customer and to an accountant — so the name is
# configured here instead of being left off the document.
#
# Cyrillic, as it appears on an ID: it is printed verbatim under „Съставил“.
# INVOICE_ISSUER_NAME=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Payments — nothing to configure (AUDIT.md Q-20)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Наложен платеж (cash on delivery) is the only payment method, by the owner's
# decision of 2026-09-20. There is no payment provider, no keys and no webhook:
# the courier collects the money and remits it. See `src/lib/payments.ts`.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Couriers (AUDIT.md Q-22, B-13/B-14)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# NOTHING HERE IS NEEDED FOR THE OFFICE PICKER.
#
# Econt's office and locker nomenclature is public: `getOffices` answers 200
# with the full production list over anonymous HTTP (verified 2026-09-16). So
# the checkout shows real offices out of the box, with no configuration.
#
# Credentials are worse than useless for that call — the endpoint validates them
# when they are present, so a typo would turn a working list into a 517 and take
# the picker down. `src/lib/couriers/econt.ts` deliberately sends none.
#
# What credentials buy is `LabelService`: **real delivery prices** today, and
# waybills, COD collection and tracking once those are built (AUDIT.md Phase 4).
# They come from a signed merchant contract.
#
# With these two and a hand-over point (below) set, the checkout asks Econt what
# each parcel costs — the real contracted tariff, the real наложен платеж fee —
# and the placeholder rate card in `src/lib/shipping.ts` is never read. Without
# them the card stands in and the checkout says so visibly. A quote that fails
# while they *are* set stops the order rather than falling back to the card: see
# `src/lib/shipping-rates.ts` for why.
#
# Econt publishes a shared demo account, so you can see live pricing before your
# own contract exists. Demo prices are the public list tariff, not your rates:
#   ECONT_ENV=demo
#   ECONT_USERNAME=iasp-dev
#   ECONT_PASSWORD=1Asp-dev
# ECONT_USERNAME=
# ECONT_PASSWORD=

# WHERE PARCELS ARE HANDED OVER. Required for pricing, and it is not a detail:
# handing the same parcel over at an office cost 4.03 EUR where having a courier
# collect it from an address cost 6.58 (real account, 2026-09-20). So there is no
# default — with none of these set, Econt is treated as unable to quote.
#
# The destination does not need configuring and does not appear here: Econt's
# office-to-office price is flat nationwide, so Sofia-to-Sofia and Sofia-to-Varna
# are the same figure.
#
# Set ONE of:
#   1. The code of the office you drop parcels at — from the picker on the site,
#      or econt.bg's office finder.
# ECONT_SENDER_OFFICE_CODE=
#   2. The address a courier collects from, all three together. Only needed when
#      that is not the registered seat in `src/lib/company.ts`, which is used
#      automatically once the owner fills it in.
# ECONT_SENDER_CITY=
# ECONT_SENDER_POST_CODE=
# ECONT_SENDER_STREET=

# WHO THE PARCEL IS FROM. Required for the admin's "Издай товарителница" button,
# and for nothing else — pricing works without it, which is how the shop ran
# before waybills existed.
#
# The phone is the whole requirement: Econt refuses a label without a sender
# phone, and `company.contact.phone` is deliberately null because the owner does
# not publish their number. Unpublished is not unknown, and the courier is not the
# open web — the number here is the one an Econt dispatcher may call about a
# parcel, so a real mobile, not the support address.
#
# ECONT_SENDER_PHONE=
#
# Optional. Defaults to the legal entity from `src/lib/company.ts`, which is what
# should be on the parcel unless you have a reason to ship under the shop name.
# ECONT_SENDER_NAME=

# WHERE THE НАЛОЖЕН ПЛАТЕЖ MONEY GOES. Optional, and leaving it unset is a
# working arrangement, not a misconfiguration: Econt then applies whatever your
# profile says, which for a personal profile means the cash waits for you at an
# office counter.
#
# Set ONE of:
#   1. A payout arrangement configured on the Econt profile ("шаблон за
#      изплащане"), referenced by its number. Preferred: the account number then
#      never travels in our requests or sits in our logs.
# ECONT_COD_PAY_TEMPLATE=
#   2. The account itself, sent with every shipment. Both halves or neither — an
#      IBAN without a BIC is rejected by Econt, so a half-filled pair is ignored
#      rather than used to fail the booking.
# ECONT_COD_IBAN=
# ECONT_COD_BIC=

# Switches the office list to Econt's demo environment. You almost certainly do
# not want this: the demo dataset has 586 offices to production's 632, **2**
# parcel lockers in the entire country against 43, and an office named
# `testtest`. It exists so that, once waybills are built, the offices you pick
# from match the dataset the demo LabelService will accept.
#
# IGNORED when NODE_ENV=production, loudly — it falls back to the real list,
# which needs no credentials, so the picker keeps working either way.
#
#   ECONT_ENV=demo
# ECONT_ENV=

# Overrides the API base URL for both environments. Only needed to point at a
# mock server; leave unset otherwise.
# ECONT_BASE_URL=

# Speedy has no public demo. Test credentials are issued by hand — email
# api@speedy.bg with your name, company and phone. Its client is still a stub
# (`courierClient('speedy')`), so setting these alone changes nothing yet.
# SPEEDY_USERNAME=
# SPEEDY_PASSWORD=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Database — Neon Postgres, EU Central / Frankfurt (AUDIT.md B-01, Q-34)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# TWO connection strings, and they are not interchangeable.
#
# DATABASE_URL is the POOLED one — the Neon host containing `-pooler`. All
# application queries use it. Serverless functions open a connection per
# invocation and would exhaust a direct connection limit under real traffic.
#
# DATABASE_URL_UNPOOLED is the DIRECT one, used only by drizzle-kit for
# migrations: DDL and migration advisory locks do not behave predictably
# through a transaction-mode pooler.
#
# They differ by one token, so you can derive either from the other:
#   direct  ...@ep-name-a1b2c3.eu-central-1.aws.neon.tech/neondb?sslmode=require
#   pooled  ...@ep-name-a1b2c3-pooler.eu-central-1.aws.neon.tech/neondb?sslmode=require
#
# The Neon integration in Vercel sets both automatically — prefer that over
# pasting them by hand.
DATABASE_URL=
DATABASE_URL_UNPOOLED=
